      "url": "https://granitepmacademy.com/",
      "name": "PMP & Project Management Certification Training | Granite PM Academy",
      "description": "PMI Premier ATP offering PMP, CAPM & CPMAI certification training. Live-virtual and on-demand formats. Certified instructors and 90-day pass guarantee.",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@id": "https://granitepmacademy.com/#website"
      },
      "about": {
        "@id": "https://granitepmacademy.com/#organization"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What are the eligibility requirements for the PMP exam?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "PMI requires a four-year degree with 36 months of project leadership experience, or a high school diploma with 60 months of experience. All applicants also need 35 hours of PM education, which our PMP Certification Training satisfies."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does it take to get PMP certified?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "After completing your training, PMI typically approves your application within 5\u201310 business days. Once approved, you have one year to schedule and pass the exam. Most candidates take 4\u20138 weeks to study after their course."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the CAPM and who should pursue it?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The Certified Associate in Project Management is designed for professionals early in their PM career or transitioning into project management. It requires only secondary education and 23 hours of training \u2014 no professional experience is required."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is CPMAI and how does it differ from PMP?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "PMI-CPMAI (PMI Certified Professional in Managing AI) focuses on managing projects that involve artificial intelligence. Built on the Cognitive Project Management for AI methodology \u2014 originally developed by Cognilytica, which PMI acquired in 2024 \u2014 it covers the AI project lifecycle, data strategy, and governance. It complements rather than replaces the PMP."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do your courses satisfy PMI\u2019s education hour requirement?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Our PMP training provides the 35 contact hours required for the PMP exam application. Our CAPM training provides the 23 hours required for the CAPM application. You receive a certificate of completion to submit to PMI."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are the courses available entirely online?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. All of our programs are offered as live-virtual cohorts conducted via video conference \u2014 no travel required. We also offer self-paced on-demand access for PMP and CAPM courses. Both formats include the same study materials and instructor support."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What work experience do I need to qualify for PMP certification?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "PMP\u00ae eligibility requires a combination of project management experience and formal education. Generally, candidates need either a bachelor's degree plus three years of project leadership experience, or a high school diploma plus five years. Specific hour requirements vary by credential level. Granite PM Academy guides you through eligibility verification and helps you document your experience for PMI\u00ae application."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is PMP certification worth the cost and time investment?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "PMP\u00ae holders report strong career advancement and competitive positioning in project-heavy industries. The credential signals expertise to employers and clients, often correlating with promotions and expanded responsibilities. While upfront costs and study time are real, the long-term ROI\u2014through career mobility, credibility, and professional growth\u2014makes it worthwhile for serious practitioners aiming to lead larger initiatives."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the difference between PMP and CAPM certification?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "CAPM\u00ae is an entry-level credential for those new to project management or with minimal experience. PMP\u00ae targets experienced project managers with documented leadership hours. PMP\u00ae carries greater industry weight and command higher market recognition. Granite PM Academy offers both pathways; CAPM\u00ae can serve as a stepping stone to PMP\u00ae, or you may qualify directly for PMP\u00ae depending on your background."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How difficult is the PMP exam and how is it structured?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The PMP\u00ae exam is rigorous, testing breadth across initiating, planning, executing, monitoring, and closing. It includes scenario-based questions that demand practical judgment, not just definitions. The exam length and question count are set by PMI\u00ae. Success requires solid training, practice exams, and hands-on review. Granite PM Academy's curriculum and mock exams are designed to close gaps and build exam confidence."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Will PMP certification help me advance in my current project management role?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Many employers prioritize PMP\u00ae for promotions to senior or executive project roles. The credential demonstrates your mastery of industry-standard frameworks and validates leadership capability. In competitive markets, PMP\u00ae often distinguishes you for higher-visibility assignments, larger budgets, and team leadership opportunities. Your current experience combined with formal certification creates a compelling profile for advancement."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

