          "name": "What work experience do I need to qualify for PMP certification?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "PMI requires applicants to demonstrate project management experience. Typically, you need a secondary degree plus three years of project management experience, or a bachelor's degree plus two years. Experience must include directing and controlling project tasks. Granite PM Academy reviews your specific background during enrollment to confirm eligibility before you enroll."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does it take to complete PMP certification training?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most PMP certification courses run four to six weeks in an intensive live-virtual format. After completing coursework and study, you'll schedule your PMP exam with PMI\u2014typically within one to three months. Total time from enrollment to exam pass varies based on your study pace and exam availability in your area."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is PMP certification worth the cost and time investment?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Run the actual numbers: Granite's live-virtual PMP Certification Training is $1,995, and PMI's own 14th Edition Earning Power Salary Survey found U.S. PMP-certified professionals earn a median of $135,000 versus $109,157 for non-certified peers \u2014 a roughly $26,000-a-year premium that recurs every year you hold the credential, not just once. Most professionals recover the training cost well within their first year of certification. Many employers also offer tuition reimbursement for professionals pursuing this certification, which can make the up-front cost close to zero."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I take PMP certification classes entirely online and live-virtual?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Granite PM Academy delivers PMP certification training via live-virtual instructor-led sessions, allowing you to participate from anywhere with internet access. This format combines real-time instruction, Q&A, and interaction with peers and instructors while maintaining the flexibility to study around your work schedule."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the difference between PMP and CAPM certifications?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "PMP (Project Management Professional) targets experienced project managers, while CAPM (Certified Associate in Project Management) is designed for entry-level professionals or those with less experience. PMP requires more work history and covers advanced concepts; CAPM has lower eligibility barriers and is often a stepping stone toward PMP. Your career stage and experience determine which is appropriate."
