            "text": "PMP PDU courses are open to current PMP\u00ae certificate holders who need to renew their credential. You do not need to hold a PMP\u00ae to take project management training courses, but PDUs (Professional Development Units) are awarded only to active PMP\u00ae professionals. Verify your certification status with PMI before enrollment to confirm eligibility for PDU credit."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I renew my PMP certification?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "PMP certification renewal happens every three years. To renew, you earn 60 PDUs (Professional Development Units) during your three-year cycle, then report them and pay PMI's renewal fee through your PMI dashboard at pmi.org. Granite PM Academy's courses are structured to help you meet your PDU requirement efficiently, well ahead of your renewal deadline."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the PMP renewal fee?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "PMI charges a separate renewal fee when you submit your PDUs for your three-year cycle \u2014 $60 for PMI members and $150 for non-members. This fee is paid directly to PMI, not to Granite PM Academy, and is separate from the cost of any PDU course you take."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are PMP PDU courses available live-virtual, or only on-demand?",
